"""Readable historical funding and offering-window audit, without return claims."""
from html import escape


def render(data):
    esc=lambda x:escape(str(x),quote=True)
    status={"verified_primary_offering":"Offering announced", "reviewed_no_primary_offering":"Reviewed: no standalone offering", "mixed_financing_boundary":"Mixed debt / equity deal", "unknown_coverage":"Coverage gap"}
    rows=[]
    for r in sorted(data["windows"],key=lambda r:(r["role"],r["ticker"],r["session"])):
        urls=list(dict.fromkeys(r["review"].get("evidence_sources",[])+r["review"].get("ir_sources",[])))
        links=" ".join(f'<a href="{esc(u)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source {i+1}</a>' for i,u in enumerate(urls))
        outcome=r["audit"]["outcome_status"]
        detail=r["review"].get("outcome_note","")
        gaps="; ".join(r["audit"]["gaps"])
        price=f'{r.get("return_60",0)*100:+.1f}% over 60 sessions; {r.get("distance_high_252",0)*100:.1f}% from annual high'
        rows.append(f'<tr data-role="{r["role"]}" data-search="{esc(r["ticker"]+" "+r["session"]+" "+status[outcome])}"><td><b>{esc(r["ticker"])}</b><small>{r["session"]}</small><small>{r["role"].capitalize()}</small></td><td><span class="badge {outcome}">{status[outcome]}</span><p>{esc(detail)}</p><small>Through {r["outcome_end"]}</small></td><td>{esc(r["review"].get("funding_note",""))}<small>{esc(price)}</small></td><td><details><summary>Review evidence</summary><p>{esc(r["review"].get("review_scope",""))}</p><p>{r["audit"]["primary_documents"]} main filings; {r["audit"]["exhibit_documents"]} linked exhibits.</p>{("<p>Open items: "+esc(gaps)+"</p>") if gaps else ""}<div class="links">{links}</div></details></td></tr>')
    s=data["stats"]
    html='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Offering research · Window audit</title><style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f3f5f5;color:#19313e;font:15px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1390px;margin:auto;padding:38px 30px 70px}.eyebrow{color:#176b63;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.13em;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase}h1{font-size:clamp(29px,4vw,46px);line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.035em;max-width:1000px;margin:15px 0}h2{font-size:23px;margin:0 0 14px}.lede{font-size:18px;color:#536b78;max-width:1000px}.meta,small{color:#5c707c;font-size:12px}small{display:block;margin-top:6px}.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:15px;margin:28px 0}.stat,section,.lesson{background:white;border:1px solid #d4dfe4;border-radius:8px;padding:23px}.stat strong{display:block;font-size:32px}.stat span{font-size:13px;color:#536b78}.lessons{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px;margin-bottom:26px}.lesson h3{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 12px}.lesson p{margin:0 0 12px}.note{background:#eaf3f0;border-left:4px solid #167467;padding:17px 21px;margin:24px 0}section{margin:24px 0}.toolbar{display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:18px}input,select{font:inherit;border:1px solid #aebdc5;padding:10px;border-radius:5px;background:white}input{width:320px;max-width:100%}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:1100px;text-align:left}th{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;background:#eff4f6}th,td{border-bottom:1px solid #d7e1e6;padding:15px 12px;vertical-align:top}td:nth-child(1){width:115px}td:nth-child(2){width:290px}td:nth-child(3){width:460px}td p{font-size:13px;margin:9px 0}.badge{font-size:12px;display:inline-block;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:5px;background:#edf2f5;font-weight:650}.verified_primary_offering{background:#e1f0e8;color:#16634c}.mixed_financing_boundary,.unknown_coverage{background:#fff1db;color:#895619}a{color:#126e63;text-underline-offset:3px}.links,.downloads{display:flex;gap:13px;flex-wrap:wrap}.links{font-size:12px;margin-top:12px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:13px}footer{font-size:13px;color:#5c707c}.empty{padding:20px;color:#5c707c}@media(max-width:750px){main{padding:22px 14px 45px}.stats{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}.stat{padding:15px}.lessons{grid-template-columns:1fr}.toolbar{display:block}.toolbar>*{display:block;width:100%;margin-top:8px}.lede{font-size:16px}section{padding:17px}}\n</style></head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">Offering research / 60-day source audit</div><h1>The audit points to three screen fixes before a larger test.</h1><p class="lede">There is one clear offering example in the original signals. The review also finds stale cash inputs, missed investments and distressed rebounds. Those issues need fixing before this pilot can say much about predictive value.</p><div class="meta">Frozen 2023–2025 sample · Reviewed __DATE__ · Free SEC and issuer sources · Research only</div>\n<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>24</strong><span>Windows: 20 original signals + 4 comparisons</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>__NEG__</strong><span>Reviewed windows with no standalone offering</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>1</strong><span>Clear offering event: Eledon, November 2025</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>__GAPS__</strong><span>Unclassified windows: issuer-release gaps</span></div></div>\n<div class="lessons"><article class="lesson"><h3>1. Require the intended price strength</h3><p>Three original signals were fresh rallies with negative 60-session returns and prices below their 50-day averages. Sarepta was still down about 74% over 60 sessions.</p><small>Derived from the frozen price observations. This is a screen-design finding, not a newly fitted trading rule.</small></article><article class="lesson"><h3>2. Verify the full liquid balance</h3><p>Fulgent’s flag used $117.6m of cash. Its filing also showed $258.2m of current marketable securities, bringing those two components to $375.8m.</p><a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1674930/000119312525271013/flgt-20250930.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fulgent filing</a><small>Excludes $411.8m of noncurrent securities. A known $67.9m later investment purchase is a separate cash use.</small></article><article class="lesson"><h3>3. Read releases before the next filing</h3><p>Sensient had already released newer cash and positive six-month free cash flow. Sarepta had published preliminary liquidity including restricted cash. The filing-only inputs missed these updates.</p><small>See the SXT July 2023 comparison and SRPT July 2025 signal below. Preserve the original assignments for this audit.</small></article></div>\n<div class="note"><b>What the outcomes mean.</b> Eledon launched its offering 11 calendar days after the October 31 signal. Sarepta’s separate $20m equity sale accompanied debt refinancing; it is shown as a mixed financing, and the same event appears in two windows. ATM programs, shelf capacity, debt and ordinary warrant exercises do not count as the frozen standalone-offering outcome.</div>\n<section><h2>Original signals and comparison windows</h2><p>No hit rate, significance test or short-return estimate is reported. Coverage gaps remain, the original sample had only one ample-cash match, and some financial/strength inputs do not represent the intended setup.</p><div class="toolbar"><input id="search" aria-label="Search audit" placeholder="Search ticker, date or outcome"><select id="role" aria-label="Choose signal or comparison"><option value="target">Original signals</option><option value="control">Comparison windows</option><option value="all">All windows</option></select><span id="count" class="meta"></span></div><div class="scroll"><table id="audit"><thead><tr><th>Observation</th><th>Next 60 calendar days</th><th>Funding and signal-quality findings</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>__ROWS__</tbody></table></div><div id="empty" class="empty" hidden>No matching windows.</div></section>\n<section><h2>What changed from the first ledger</h2><p>A newly recovered January 10, 2023 Geron closing release confirms approximately $213.3m of estimated net proceeds before its January 31 signal. Its prior “receipt unconfirmed” status reflected missing source coverage. The old ledger remains preserved.</p><a href="https://ir.geron.com/news-releases/news-release-details/geron-corporation-announces-closing-upsized-public-offering" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Geron closing release</a><p>Intellia also had a $30m licensing receipt in April 2024, disclosed in May, and a much smaller $307,000 ATM settlement in July 2025, disclosed in August. Later quarterly ATM sales are retained as retrospective outcome evidence and are not inserted into earlier signal-time cash.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1652130/000095017024057046/ntla-20240331.htm">Intellia April receipt</a><a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1652130/000095017025104987/ntla-20250630.htm">Intellia July settlement</a></div></section>\n<section><h2>Audit scope and reproducibility</h2><p>__DOCS__ captured SEC documents, including linked exhibits and covering financial statements. Review checks include the complete selected filing inventory, financial/equity notes and independent issuer release listings. Reviewed negatives are bounded to these selected sources, not proof of universal absence. A keyword search alone cannot establish a negative. Sources received after a signal can validate later events, but cannot update cash information at that earlier signal.</p><p>Mixed debt/equity transactions retain both inclusive and strict standalone interpretations in the audit files. The two Sarepta windows also lack complete independent release chronologies, so their strict standalone outcomes remain unknown. Neither is silently substituted for the frozen definition. The original 90-company cohort and all 20 signals remain unchanged.</p><div class="downloads"><a href="audited_windows.csv">Window audit</a><a href="reviewed_windows.json">Source review notes</a><a href="audited_events.json">Event identities</a><a href="captured_documents.json">Document inventory</a><a href="audit_protocol.json">Frozen audit scope</a><a href="manifest.json">Verification evidence</a></div></section>\n<footer>Next: repair investment/release coverage and define a new screen that excludes damaged rebounds before freezing a larger test. This audit does not validate a trading strategy or alter the live strategy book.</footer></main><script>\nconst rows=[...document.querySelectorAll(\'#audit tbody tr\')];function filter(){const q=document.querySelector(\'#search\').value.trim().toLowerCase(),role=document.querySelector(\'#role\').value;let n=0;for(const r of rows){r.hidden=!(r.dataset.search.toLowerCase().includes(q)&&(role===\'all\'||r.dataset.role===role));if(!r.hidden)n++;}document.querySelector(\'#count\').textContent=n+\' of 24 windows\';document.querySelector(\'#empty\').hidden=n>0;}document.querySelector(\'#search\').addEventListener(\'input\',filter);document.querySelector(\'#role\').addEventListener(\'change\',filter);filter();\n</script></body></html>'
    values=dict(DATE=data["generated_at"][:10],NEG=s["status_counts"].get("reviewed_no_primary_offering",0),GAPS=s["status_counts"].get("unknown_coverage",0),DOCS=s["captured_documents"],ROWS="".join(rows))
    for k,v in values.items():html=html.replace("__"+k+"__",str(v))
    return html
